Our changes to LSd's C source, applied onto upstream's at image build
time (Dockerfile). The lsd submodule itself stays upstream's: make a
change in lsd/, `git -C lsd diff > patches/lsd/NNNN-name.patch`, then
`git -C lsd checkout -- .`. dev/bump-lsd.sh checks every patch still
applies to the new upstream.

  0001-steady-tick.patch  the main loop waits for the next tick in naps
                          of at most 1 ms instead of one sleep, and drops
                          missed ticks past 3 behind instead of running
                          them back to back: a steady 60 ticks a second
                          where the OS wakes sleepers late (Docker
                          Desktop's VM: 16 ms sleeps woke up to 160 ms
                          late, clients saw 10 then 110 updates a
                          second). Worth offering upstream.
